# Read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages; other hosts serve it as a plain file and ignore it.
# The same old addresses are also built as instant-forward pages (redirects in astro.config.mjs), so they work
# on any host; these rules answer with a real one-hop 301 where the host applies them first. Don't add Netlify's
# "301!" force suffix: Cloudflare rejects the whole rule.
#
# "/join/*" also covers /join/ and the retired /join/thanks/ form page. On Netlify a splat matches its own base
# path too, so never point a "/x/*" rule back at "/x" (v1.5.0 did, and the rule never fired); here the target is
# a different page, so that's fine. Targets use /connect/ (with the slash) so there's no second 301.
/events     /connect/#events  301
/events/*   /connect/#events  301
/join       /connect/#join    301
/join/*     /connect/#join    301
